  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<p>Correct answer: B</p>\n<p>A: This would be the result of using half the peak voltage (<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V = 10\\ \\text{V}\"></span>) in <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P = V^2 / R\"></span>.</p>\n<p>B: Peak voltage <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V_0 = 20\\ \\text{V}\"></span>.<br/><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V_{rms} = \\frac{20}{\\sqrt{2}}\\ \\text{V}\"></span>.<br/>Average power <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P = \\frac{V_{rms}^2}{R} = \\frac{(20/\\sqrt{2})^2}{10} = \\frac{400}{20} = 20\\ \\text{W}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>C: This assumes peak voltage is the RMS voltage: <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P = \\frac{V_0^2}{R} = \\frac{400}{10} = 40\\ \\text{W}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>D: This results from using the peak-to-peak voltage (<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"40\\ \\text{V}\"></span>) as the voltage in the power formula.</p>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_1a",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The graph shows the variation with time <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t\"></span> of the voltage <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V\"></span> across a <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"10\\ \\Omega\"></span> resistor.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>What is the average power dissipated in the resistor?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"10\\ \\text{W}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"20\\ \\text{W}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"40\\ \\text{W}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"80\\ \\text{W}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
